From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:06:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: Register the A733 GPU_CORE
 domain by its state

GPU_CORE is flagged always-on, so the driver reports it on whatever its
PPU says. On the Cubie A7S its PPU reads off from boot until the GPU
driver binds, which powers the domain through the GPU clock, its bus
gate and its reset rather than through the PPU. A consumer attached to
GPU_CORE on the strength of that report would reach an unpowered block,
and an access there stops the SoC without a message.

Drop the always-on flag. GPU_CORE is then registered in the state its
PPU reports, as every other A733 domain.

The PPU does not switch this domain by its policy. It comes on once
the GPU PLL, the GPU module clock and the bus gate with the reset
released are all on, and it stays on afterwards, also while GPU_TOP is
off and with the policy written to off. A consumer must therefore not
attach GPU_CORE: power_on() would wait for a status that the domain
only reaches after the consumer has clocked the block, and time out.
The GPU node uses GPU_TOP only.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: GPU_CORE registers off as its PPU reads,
the GPU still binds, renders and runtime-suspends, no power transition
reaches the controller while sync_state is pending, and with the GPU
suspended the PPU keeps GPU_CORE on after its policy is written to off.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
index 72b5cb79d358..6784d642360f 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ static const struct sunxi_pck600_desc sun55i_a523_pck600_desc = {
 
 static const struct sunxi_pck600_pd_desc sun60i_a733_pck600_pds[] = {
 	{ "VI", }, { "DE_SYS", }, { "VE_DEC", }, { "VE_ENC", }, { "NPU", },
-	{ "GPU_TOP", }, { "GPU_CORE", GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON },
+	{ "GPU_TOP", }, { "GPU_CORE", },
 	{ "PCIE", }, { "USB2", }, { "VO", }, { "VO1", },
 };
 
